==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*8 [[Zroco]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*3 [[Zigge]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*3 [[Zang Roo]]s spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*2 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 86.67 seconds<sup>2,600f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This level is easily rushable, since the base has low HP and the Zang Roos and Aku Gories spawn on a timer. To rush it, simply wait until the first Aku Doge spawns, then break its [[Shield]] with either [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] or another cat strong enough to do so in one hit. Once its' Shield is broken, kill the Aku Doge with [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Express Cat]], then save up money for Awakened Bahamut. Bahamut shouldn't have much trouble reaching and destroying the enemy base when aided by meatshields.

